Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 22:22:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Part I directional/sign audit: root-cause the fixed-dual
 vs reoptimized opposite-sign observation

Traces to an extra unary minus in overnight_cm_cplus_d4_gate.jl's own Section 4
ground-truth secant construction (true_secant = -(Dp-Dm)/(2h) instead of
(Dp-Dm)/(2h)), not a defect in the production fixed-dual Jacobian. Independently
re-derived the sign convention from source (cb_F!/cb_G!/lfix_from_q/pivot_expand),
added a base-point value sanity check the prior derivation lacked, and ran two new
batteries: a 28-row bandwidth/winner-stability sweep (4 coordinates x 7 h values)
and a 32-row directional-prediction sweep (4 directions x 8 magnitudes). Both show
28/28 and 32/32 correct sign agreement once the harness bug is fixed, including
deep into winner-switch-heavy territory (up to 60 switches) -- no genuine
smooth-point sign failure found. Fixed the bug in the actual gate test and added
an explicit sign-agreement check; 54/54 pass (up from 48/48).

See docs/CM_FIXED_DUAL_VS_REOPTIMIZED_DIRECTIONAL_AUDIT_2026-07-23.md.

